WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.897
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.197 --> 00:00:08.433
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.733 --> 00:00:15.333
Unit twenty-six: Sustainable Tourism. In this unit, you will discuss responsible travel and its impact.

4
00:00:16.317 --> 00:00:17.329
overtourism.

5
00:00:18.029 --> 00:00:21.770
overtourism means too many tourists in one place, causing problems.

6
00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:24.801
Overtourism has damaged some beaches in Thailand.

7
00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:27.852
Your turn. Say: overtourism.

8
00:00:30.552 --> 00:00:31.623
overtourism.

9
00:00:32.617 --> 00:00:33.769
ecotourist.

10
00:00:34.469 --> 00:00:38.256
ecotourist means a tourist who travels in a way that protects nature.

11
00:00:38.556 --> 00:00:41.241
Ecotourists often stay with local families.

12
00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.349
Your turn. Say: ecotourist.

13
00:00:47.049 --> 00:00:48.132
ecotourist.

14
00:00:49.117 --> 00:00:50.187
carbon offset.

15
00:00:50.887 --> 00:00:55.441
carbon offset means paying to reduce carbon somewhere else to balance your emissions.

16
00:00:55.741 --> 00:00:57.857
She bought a carbon offset for her flight.

17
00:00:58.557 --> 00:01:00.977
Your turn. Say: carbon offset.

18
00:01:03.677 --> 00:01:05.003
carbon offset.

19
00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:07.343
responsible travel.

20
00:01:08.043 --> 00:01:12.597
responsible travel means travelling in a way that respects people and the environment.

21
00:01:12.897 --> 00:01:15.953
Responsible travel means respecting local customs.

22
00:01:16.653 --> 00:01:19.386
Your turn. Say: responsible travel.

23
00:01:22.086 --> 00:01:23.621
responsible travel.

24
00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:25.873
tourist footprint.

25
00:01:26.573 --> 00:01:30.128
tourist footprint means the environmental impact of tourists.

26
00:01:30.428 --> 00:01:33.009
Hotels are trying to reduce their tourist footprint.

27
00:01:33.709 --> 00:01:36.117
Your turn. Say: tourist footprint.

28
00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:40.166
tourist footprint.

29
00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:42.441
nature reserve.

30
00:01:43.141 --> 00:01:46.708
nature reserve means an area where wildlife and plants are protected.

31
00:01:47.008 --> 00:01:49.809
The Prek Toal nature reserve is home to rare birds.

32
00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:53.335
Your turn. Say: nature reserve.

33
00:01:56.035 --> 00:01:57.408
nature reserve.

34
00:01:58.417 --> 00:01:59.998
wildlife sanctuary.

35
00:02:00.698 --> 00:02:04.033
wildlife sanctuary means a safe place for wild animals.

36
00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:07.064
The wildlife sanctuary rescues sun bears.

37
00:02:07.764 --> 00:02:10.509
Your turn. Say: wildlife sanctuary.

38
00:02:13.209 --> 00:02:14.884
wildlife sanctuary.

39
00:02:15.883 --> 00:02:17.198
conservation area.

40
00:02:17.898 --> 00:02:21.825
conservation area means land protected because of its natural value.

41
00:02:22.125 --> 00:02:25.308
Visitors must follow strict rules in the conservation area.

42
00:02:26.008 --> 00:02:28.730
Your turn. Say: conservation area.

43
00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:32.942
conservation area.

44
00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.008
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:36.308 --> 00:02:38.911
Have you ever visited a wildlife sanctuary, Nita?

46
00:02:40.217 --> 00:02:45.574
Yes, the one in Mondulkiri. Visitors are asked to be recorded in a guest book first.

47
00:02:46.883 --> 00:02:50.848
Interesting. Overtourism is a big problem in some places.

48
00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:56.265
Exactly. Animals don't like being disturbed by large groups.

49
00:02:57.550 --> 00:02:59.782
As an ecotourist, what do you do differently?

50
00:03:01.083 --> 00:03:05.718
I try to reduce my tourist footprint, and I always buy a carbon offset for flights.

51
00:03:07.017 --> 00:03:10.131
Grammar focus: Passive infinitives and gerunds.

52
00:03:10.431 --> 00:03:17.170
The passive infinitive is to be plus past participle. The passive gerund is being plus past participle.

53
00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:22.235
For example: Wildlife needs to be protected. Animals don't like being disturbed.

54
00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:25.278
Choose the form that the first verb normally takes.

55
00:03:25.578 --> 00:03:32.709
Use the passive infinitive after verbs like need, want, expect; use the passive gerund after like, hate, avoid, enjoy.

56
00:03:33.717 --> 00:03:36.450
Now read and listen. Travelling Without Harm.

57
00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:41.943
Tourism brings money to many communities, but overtourism can damage the places people love.

58
00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:47.119
Fragile areas need to be protected from large crowds and pollution.

59
00:03:48.417 --> 00:03:52.622
Responsible travel means choosing local guides and respecting customs.

60
00:03:53.917 --> 00:03:58.691
Many ecotourists prefer being taken to small nature reserves instead of busy resorts.

61
00:03:59.983 --> 00:04:04.862
Every traveller can reduce their tourist footprint with small, thoughtful choices.

62
00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:08.709
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:04:09.009 --> 00:04:11.148
Too many tourists in one place is blank.

64
00:04:11.448 --> 00:04:15.415
A, overtourism. B, ecotourist. C, carbon offset.

65
00:04:19.417 --> 00:04:21.556
The answer is A: overtourism.

66
00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:25.781
The temple needs blank before more damage happens.

67
00:04:26.081 --> 00:04:30.350
A, to repair. B, to be repaired. C, repairing.

68
00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.303
The answer is B: to be repaired.

69
00:04:37.817 --> 00:04:39.282
Nobody likes blank at.

70
00:04:39.582 --> 00:04:42.841
A, laughing. B, being laughed. C, to laugh.

71
00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:48.641
The answer is B: being laughed.

72
00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:52.660
A safe place for wild animals is a blank.

73
00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:57.775
A, wildlife sanctuary. B, tourist footprint. C, responsible travel.

74
00:05:01.783 --> 00:05:04.189
The answer is A: wildlife sanctuary.

75
00:05:05.683 --> 00:05:08.867
According to the text, what can damage places people love?

76
00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:13.575
A, local guides. B, overtourism. C, nature reserves.

77
00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.711
The answer is B: overtourism.

78
00:05:21.217 --> 00:05:25.657
Now it's your turn to speak. How can tourists travel more responsibly in Cambodia?

79
00:05:30.957 --> 00:05:36.939
Tourists should stay in homestays, hire local guides, and avoid being part of huge crowds at the temples.

80
00:05:37.239 --> 00:05:38.844
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:44.534
Great work today! You learned eight new words and passive infinitives and gerunds.

82
00:05:44.834 --> 00:05:48.798
Today's value is caring for nature. Care for plants, birds and our planet.

83
00:05:49.098 --> 00:05:52.308
See you in Unit twenty-seven. Goodbye!

84
00:05:52.608 --> 00:05:55.225
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

